THOUGHT: I need to make `bindSide` robust to a nullable `side` parameter to satisfy NullAway. The simplest fix is to add a null check and return early if `side` is null, which is safe given `getSide()` can return null. After that, I must rerun the Gradle compile to ensure the build succeeds and that no additional NullAway errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '179,185c\  protected void bindSide(@Nullable final Cubemap.CubemapSide side) {
    if (side == null) {
      return;
    }
    Gdx.gl20.glFramebufferTexture2D(
        GL20.GL_FRAMEBUFFER,
        GL20.GL_COLOR_ATTACHMENT0,
        side.glEnum,
        getColorBufferTexture().getTextureObjectHandle(),
        0);
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/glutils/FrameBufferCubemap.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

